WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.520
Ladies and gentlemen, today we're
testing our new drone, which is

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.760
the DJI Mini 5 Pro.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.680
It launches today, DJI sent
it to us to test, and we had

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.080
a really stupid idea.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.240
We turned to our friend Mari,
the reckless one who took

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.440
us on a hike up a mountain
that nearly gave half the group

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.600
a heart attack, and we
told her: pick a trail for

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.960
all of us to do, and
we'll fly the drone there.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.280
She said: sure thing.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.160
But this morning she texted
us: bring snacks, extra water,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.619
a hoodie, emergency gear, a bear whistle.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.760
If you don't know DJI's
Mini line, it's a line of

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.920
drones that weigh less than 250 grams.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.560
Why? Because in many countries
you don't need a pilot's license

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.880
to fly a 250-gram drone.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.720
Here in Canada, for example, you don't.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.520
Not in Europe either.
Why 250 grams?

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.560
Because the top speed it reaches
when it falls isn't enough

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.560
to hurt anyone.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.000
Smart. But every year they
really blow us away with the tech

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.440
they manage to pack into these drones.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.120
Wow, look at the size of this kit.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.120
And this year the thing is insane.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.160
Here we've got the Fly More Combo version.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.800
You can find it in other versions
too, but this is the one with

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:19.919
the most stuff. It's the most complete.
Including a bunch of accessories.

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:22.400
Here's our drone, and there's
a lot of stuff in here too.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.240
And the charger.
And the battery.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.440
Wow, what a cute little bag, huh?

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.840
This one's bigger than
the others, actually.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.819
Yep. It comes ready to fly.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.200
Here we go. It comes with the
controller version that has the

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.999
built-in screen, because there's a
slightly cheaper one, but you have

00:01:37.039 --> 00:01:38.760
to hook your smartphone up to it.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.360
It also comes with a battery kit, 3
in total, the other one's inside the

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.440
drone. It also comes with ND filters

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.399
and a bunch of spare propellers,
in case you, you know...

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.160
Inevitably, right?
Good call, good call.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.560
But let's talk about the drone first.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.060
It's held by a single
piece that goes around

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.740
here. Just one, you can't get it
wrong, and it opens like this.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.240
Oops, there's a card in there.
Take the little paper off.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.560
Yeah, exactly. It unfolds like this.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.960
And it's already on. It turns right on.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.599
You can... you have the option for it
to power on as soon as you unfold it,

00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:13.720
and that's the default setting.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.040
You can change that later.
The most impressive thing about it.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:22.040
First, like other models, it has
that 360 camera that's there to see

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.440
around it. It's not for filming,
it's to keep you from crashing into

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.040
things. That's very important.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.000
But on top of that, this model
also has LiDAR on the front.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.400
What does that let you do?

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.960
You can avoid collisions
and crashes in low light.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.440
Basically, you can fly at night
with just streetlights, and

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.040
it'll be able to stop if it's
about to hit something in front.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.540
Thank you, DJI. And the most amazing
thing, if you know anything about filming,

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.920
you'll get really excited now, it's
something you only got in drones

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.200
that were heavier and pricier, but it's
arriving, as far as I know, for the first

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.960
time in a drone under
250 grams: its sensor.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.040
It has a 1-inch sensor,
which for a drone this

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.160
size is a gigantic sensor.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.560
By increasing the physical size of
the sensor, it's a 1-inch sensor and

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.800
50 megapixels, you also
increase the image quality.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.200
You go from that image that looks
like it's from a cheap phone to

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.040
a point-and-shoot camera,
that level, you know?

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.680
Better, a bit better. It has a
longer-lasting battery, plus a gimbal that

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.520
rotates up to 225 degrees, so we're going
to get some really cool shots, okay?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.160
And it also works for vertical video.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.680
And another amazing thing: if
you've got batteries from the

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.560
Mini 3 or Mini 4 line,
they work on it too.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.600
So...

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.179
And here's a physical comparison
with the 4. On the 4 you had 2

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.980
pieces to protect it, which is
this here, and then you have to

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.240
take this off too.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.440
On this one, as you saw, it's all one
piece, which I found super interesting.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.880
Very practical. And with the 4,
first off, you have a camera with a

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.760
smaller sensor. Wow.
You can see the size there, you can tell.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.200
You can really compare them.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:03.200
Exactly. And you also don't have
the LiDAR sensors here on the front.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.680
That's the big... one
of the big differences.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.440
It also has internal storage, in
case you leave your card at home, and

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.480
it also has a new ND filter system.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.840
An ND filter is this thing that's like
sunglasses for your lens, basically

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.000
to control how much light gets
in, and in some situations you'll

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.239
want to do that.
On this one it's press-fit.

00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:25.840
Snap. You just put it on, snap it
in, and to take it off, you just

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.640
pull. Be careful.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.780
What kind of mess is Mari
going to get us into?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.840
So we went on a trail picked by
Mari and her boyfriend, John.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.200
They're both very experienced hikers,
and John is an ultramarathoner.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.760
We went to Squamish, near
Vancouver, and the plan was

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.619
to climb a peak called Slhanay.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.600
Sila, Sila, Shlaha, Shilahai?

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.160
Sorry, I don't know how to pronounce it.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.799
But right as we got there, we
were really lucky to come across a

00:04:53.839 --> 00:04:56.040
natural phenomenon to film with the drone.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.840
Every two years, from what
I was told, in that area,

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.720
pink salmon swim up the river to spawn.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:06.460
It's tons of saltwater salmon
going up the river to spawn up

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.120
there, and then they die.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.000
It's because they can't survive in
fresh water, they're saltwater fish,

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.880
there's probably a better
explanation than that, sorry.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:17.560
Then we found a spot where the
salmon were gathered, resting

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.280
apparently, because in some parts of the
river these pools form, and they stay

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.440
there for a while to
get their energy back.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.239
So I put the drone up to
show the scene in a way that

00:05:27.279 --> 00:05:32.239
only a drone can, because I
flew right above the fish.

00:05:32.279 --> 00:05:36.799
You get that panorama, you see all
the fish gathered, it's really cool.

00:05:36.839 --> 00:05:39.960
And it was actually the first
time I'd seen this phenomenon up

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.840
close. I live in British Columbia,
Canada, and this happens here from

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.799
time to time, with more
than one species of salmon.

00:05:47.839 --> 00:05:51.760
But when I got there, totally
unplanned, we saw all of this

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.040
happening, this natural phenomenon,
and I had the drone with me.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.880
The footage came out really good.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.040
It's footage I shoot for the video,
but afterwards it goes on my NAS

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.960
because I want to keep it forever, because
I want to rewatch it in the future,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.120
right? But anyway, we're here to talk
about the drone, this is a review.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.280
Let's stop talking about fish.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.900
And the first of the drone's
new features I tried to test was

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.160
its obstacle detection, whether
it really stops before hitting

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.699
something. And most importantly,
whether with the LiDAR it stops

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.160
even in places without ideal
lighting, which was the case

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.760
where we were, because
there was a lot of shade.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.160
By default, it stops
before it hits things.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.879
It really was stopping.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:37.000
It stopped. But you can switch it to
dodge things on its own, and that's

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.860
what I wanted to test, because
you can have it follow you through

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.300
the trees and it sort of
dodges everything, in theory.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.539
Dodge, dodge, dodge, dodge, dodge.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.680
And sure enough, its motion
detection system works.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.120
Like, these small drones
didn't have this, okay?

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:56.379
It worked, but you needed good lighting.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.760
Now I trust it a lot more, okay?

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.480
A lot more. But then we had
to do the hike, didn't we?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:07.160
My plan was to reach the top of
the mountain and fly the drone

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.300
up there at sunset, the golden
hour, as everyone calls it, which

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.920
is the best time to film anything.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.880
If you saw the Cadê a Chave
video where we cover this whole

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:19.000
adventure, you know
that's not how it went.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:24.520
It was a brutal trail, ridiculously
high, in a place with no infrastructure

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:28.800
at all, the kind of trail with nothing
marked, nothing prepared, you only

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.680
know you can make it because
someone experienced is up front

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.880
showing you where to step.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:35.920
But sooner or later you're
stumbling around, grabbing onto tree

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.660
roots, pulling yourself
up, climbing rocks, and

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.040
I did all that carrying the drone,
which isn't very heavy, 250 grams

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:46.280
plus the controller, no complaints there,
I had some extra batteries too, but

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.699
I also had to carry the DSLR camera

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.259
and my tripod.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.680
Anyway, we got to the top and I really
wanted to test some more features

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.680
and the drone's image quality,
except I was dead, okay?

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.360
Dead, dead, dead.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.120
Metaphorically, right? Because I'm
alive here, you can see me, I'm not

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.960
a ghost. So what did I do?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:11.060
I put the drone on auto, 100%
auto, the drone was deciding all

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:12.640
the exposure and white balance for me.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.240
The only thing I did differently
was shoot in D-Log M, because it

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.560
also has a log format so you can
work with it in post and choose

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.360
the color later. Like, the image comes
out like this and you can add color

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.859
afterwards like this, which
is great for post-production.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.200
But anyway, everything was on auto, okay?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.219
If you want to know how the
camera behaves when you know

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.940
absolutely nothing about filming and let
it decide everything for you, this is

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.360
your chance to see it.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.880
You'll also get to see the drone
filming in low light, because we

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.240
got there a bit later than I wanted, okay?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.120
The sun was already setting,
the golden hour was almost over.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:52.320
So we've got a few unintentional
tests in there, okay?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.260
I tested one of its features
for pre-programmed moves.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.840
You can do some automatic moves with
the drone while it tracks you or

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.440
tracks something else.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.960
That's not new with this drone,
but what is new is that the

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:09.920
tracking system works much
better, way better than what I saw

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.700
on the Mini 3 Pro or the Mini 4 Pro.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.400
You lock it on, and I haven't managed
to make it lose the target yet.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.040
And another really cool thing
is that you can turn its

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.880
camera up to 225 degrees, which
gives you vertical video that doesn't

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:29.920
lose resolution, since you don't have
to crop a horizontal sensor. Its camera

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.840
actually rotates, and you can also
do shots like this one, with the

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.880
drone moving backwards and the
camera rotating at the same time.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.519
That's me sitting there
controlling everything, okay?

00:09:40.559 --> 00:09:43.560
It's all manual there, but it's
a really cool shot, alright?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.600
Really cool. And the most impressive
part is that up at the top of the

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:49.720
mountain it was super windy, crazy windy.

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:53.920
We were in a place called Squamish,
which means place of the wind, or place

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.120
where there's wind, sorry,
something like that, okay?

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.480
It has to do with wind, and
it totally lives up to it.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:03.519
And watching the drone in that wind,
it was struggling, really struggling,

00:10:03.559 --> 00:10:08.600
you know? It was hard to keep it steady,
but when you look at its footage,

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.000
you'd never guess it was windy.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.840
I don't know what kind
of witchcraft this is.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:15.200
There's also this cool bit: if you
point that little camera at it, you can

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.920
see the LiDAR blinking. You can't see it
with the naked eye, but the camera can.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.680
But then we had to put the
drone back in the backpack, the

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.880
camera too, and nearly die going
down that mountain in the dark.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.840
It's in the Cadê a Chave
video, if you haven't seen it.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:31.020
But did I get everything
I wanted that day?

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:33.400
Absolutely not. Would I have liked to?

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:36.960
Yes. Did I skip it because I
nearly died climbing the mountain?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.680
Yes. But then, on another
sunny day, we went to a place

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.960
here in Vancouver called Deep Cove.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.440
First, because the government lets you fly
a drone there without a license, if it's

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:49.360
under 250 grams, and also
because I can fly over the

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.960
water, because one of the rules
here is no flying over people.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.299
Respect the law, first and foremost.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.620
And right after we took off,
I had to do this test with

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:02.000
Nilce that I saw someone else
do online: the camera's sensor

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:05.960
is so big, this 1-inch
sensor, that it has to focus

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.380
on different planes.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:11.120
So we played around in front of
the camera with the drone's focus.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:15.160
I found that impressive, because
cameras with a really small sensor, like

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.800
this one here, an action
camera, a GoPro, don't focus.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:23.380
It basically has infinite focus
past a certain distance, the sensor

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.240
is so small that everything's in focus.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.120
Usually that's 30, 20, 40 centimeters.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.920
So there's no focusing work at all.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.000
The drone does focus.
That's a good thing, okay?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.339
That, that's, that's a
plus, it's just, uh...

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:40.160
Let's continue. I did another
tracking test using my assistant.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:45.240
Actually, I tagged Nilce on the
controller and had the drone follow

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:49.960
her. I basically just held the stick
forward and the drone kept following

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:54.280
her, dodging trees, and
she was glued to the drone.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.280
Metaphorically, I mean that in the
sense that the drone's tracking didn't

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.920
lose her. I gave her some
directions, told her to go up,

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.440
down, that kind of thing.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.120
I tried to make the drone
lose her and it didn't.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.600
And it did that while dodging
trees, because I was flying

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:13.840
really low. I also used the
Deep Cove trip to compare

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:18.020
the Mini 5 Pro with the Mini
4 Pro, the previous model.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.320
What's the difference in the image?

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:24.280
I flew both drones and
turned them back toward us.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.840
Honestly, when I looked at it later
on the computer at home, I didn't see

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:30.800
much difference in dynamic
range in this scene.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:34.639
However, overall I found the
5's image quality much better.

00:12:34.679 --> 00:12:39.160
It's footage I'd intercut
with a much bigger camera.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:42.519
I don't see the need to bring
a bigger drone than this to get

00:12:42.559 --> 00:12:44.120
higher-quality footage.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:48.220
In that sense, it really impressed me,
but the Mini 4 Pro's image was already

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:52.120
good enough for 95% of cases.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:56.639
You could probably put its
footage on TV, for example, and

00:12:56.679 --> 00:13:00.000
nobody would think it came
from a 250-gram drone.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.939
So the Mini 4, in that sense,

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:05.560
is very good. But since both
drones were up, we tried

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.240
to film one with the other,
which is kind of tricky.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:12.240
You can't do it by eye, you have
to check the measuring tools

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.120
and so on, on the controller, and
try to match one to the other.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.280
But it worked, okay?

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.240
It worked. Yes, yes, yes,
we can see it, Nilce,

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:25.219
we can see it. But the most important
test is shooting into the sun.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:29.160
I pointed both drones at this
area with a forest below,

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:32.840
some trees and so on, with the
sun blazing above, and I'll tell

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:38.360
you, here the Mini 5 held
on to way more detail in the

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.680
shadows, and I mean way more.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.080
In that sense, the DJI
Mini 5 is much better.

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:48.000
Its image quality in this scene is
also much better when you look at

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.240
the boats and so on.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:52.360
One more thing I noticed,
and I'm not sure if it's

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:56.040
really the Mini 5 or
because it was in a slightly

00:13:56.080 --> 00:14:00.440
different position from the Mini 4,
but in the Mini 5's image you can see

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.480
some light leaking in.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.519
You can see the light hit the
lens and there's a bit of flare.

00:14:05.559 --> 00:14:09.400
I wasn't using the ND filter, it's
just the drone's camera, and that's

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:13.840
the difference. And finally, when
I sent both drones back to land,

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:17.800
the 5 came back showing off
its obstacle detection again.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:23.080
Because the 4 is less confident,
it climbs way up to God knows

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:27.360
where to avoid trees, avoid everything,
gets roughly to the spot where

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.680
it has to land, since it saves
the GPS location to do that

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:32.880
automatically, and then it comes down.

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:36.600
But it really comes from way up there,
it climbs all that out of fear of trees.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.900
Meanwhile the 5 shows up like: dude,

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:40.920
dude, I know how to do this, okay?

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.480
I know, I know, I'm not
scared, I know how to do this.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.480
All the confidence in the
world, couldn't care less.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:47.440
It came in and landed.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:51.140
But I'm genuinely impressed with
the DJI Mini 5 Pro, because it

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.720
has amazing image quality
for its size, with a sensor

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.600
we'd never have imagined
in a drone this light.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:02.600
It might not be a worthwhile upgrade
from the Mini 4 Pro if you're

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.220
happy with the Mini 4 Pro's image quality

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:09.000
or if you just fly above
everything and don't have to

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.600
worry about any obstacles.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.320
Some people just put the
drone way up high, okay?

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.400
Nothing to hit, off it goes. But then
there are the crazies flying through

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:17.560
the middle of the trees, right?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:21.000
If the image quality and obstacle
detection aren't something

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:25.400
that justifies the price for you, the
4 is still very good, it's exceptional.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.360
The 4 is very good, okay?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:30.800
The 4 is very good, but man,
that 1-inch sensor on the 5,

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.760
the image is sensational, my friend.

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.120
And mind you, I've flown every
one of these drones, okay?

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.600
I've been flying them since
the very first 250-gram one.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:41.560
I've been flying drones here in Canada
for years, never got a license, I can only

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.680
fly up to 250 grams,
there's no other option.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:46.520
And this jump in image quality
on the 5 is the biggest I've

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.200
seen from one generation to
the next so far, I think.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:52.840
There was a huge jump from the
2 to the 3 Pro, but I won't

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:56.720
count that one, because alongside
the 3 Pro they released a non-Pro 3

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.760
as well, with image
quality closer to the 2's.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:02.020
So I'm giving the crown to the 5, okay?

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:05.000
But it's impressive, truly impressive.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:07.720
So that's my review. Don't
forget to drop a like if

